---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Vemor Comps Pilot Program — Trial Terms"
  description="Terms for the Vemor Comps pilot program: 30-day evaluation access for participating attorneys."
  path="/trial-terms"
  hideWidget={true}
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:24px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">Vemor Comps</span>
    <h1>Pilot Program.<br /><span class="gold">Trial terms.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Plain-English terms for evaluation access to Vemor Comps. Using the platform
      during the pilot means you're good with these.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="prose" style="max-width:800px;">
        <h2>1. What this is</h2>
        <p>
          Vemor Consulting LLC ("Vemor") is providing you evaluation access to the
          Vemor Comps platform at no charge, so you can assess it in your own
          practice. The pilot runs for the period stated in your welcome email
          (generally 30 days from your first login). When it ends, access ends
          unless your firm has entered a subscription.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Informational use only</h2>
        <p>
          Vemor Comps is an informational reference built from publicly filed
          documents. It is not legal advice, no attorney-client relationship is
          created, and Vemor is not a law firm. Figures are verified against source
          documents under our published <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>, but
          you should independently verify any figure before relying on it in a
          proceeding, negotiation, or mediation — the source filings are delivered
          with every report precisely so you can.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Your access</h2>
        <p>
          Access is individual, tied to your email address, and non-transferable —
          please don't share login links or downloaded reports outside your firm.
          Reports you generate during the pilot are licensed for use in your
          matters and your firm's internal analysis.
        </p>
        <p>
          Usage is logged. Sign-ins, searches, and reports generated are recorded
          against your email address and are visible to Vemor and your firm's pilot
          sponsor. Anything shared more widely within your firm is reported in
          aggregate, not by individual.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Communications</h2>
        <p>
          As a pilot participant you'll receive occasional product updates about
          Vemor Comps, and — when it launches — Vemor's legal-intelligence briefing
          (a short digest of newly published California appellate and Ninth Circuit
          opinions relevant to your practice). We keep it useful and infrequent, and
          we never share your email. Prefer not to receive the briefing or updates?
          One line to <a href="mailto:comps@vemor.ai">comps@vemor.ai</a> — or the
          unsubscribe link in any email — and you're out, no questions.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          Part of the point of a pilot: tell us what's missing, confusing, or
          wrong. Vemor may use feedback you provide to improve the product, with
          no obligation or attribution. If you spot a figure you believe is
          incorrect, we want to know the same day —
          <a href="mailto:comps@vemor.ai">comps@vemor.ai</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>6. The boring-but-necessary part</h2>
        <p>
          Evaluation access is provided "as is" during the pilot. Vemor may modify,
          suspend, or end the pilot or any account at its discretion. Our standard
          <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> apply to the extent not modified
          here. No fees are owed for the pilot period — full stop.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:32px; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem;">
          Questions: <a href="mailto:comps@vemor.ai">comps@vemor.ai</a> ·
          Vemor Consulting LLC, San Diego, CA
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
